0036:     Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.
0037: 
0038:     Input structure:
0039:     - bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.
0040: 
0041:     Rule:
0042:     - For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.
0043:     - Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.
0044: 
0045:     Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.
0046:     """
